Source patch for the GNU build layer only -- tools/makeprom.c, tools/makedi.c,
os/unix/fsys.c, os/unix/wrapper.c.

Nine printf conversions whose width matched the ILP32 ABI this code was
written for and not LP64. In the tools: %lx for the `int size` OBMD/dropin
header fields (four sites), %x for a pointer difference (two: `here-start`,
`insert_ptr-prom`, now cast to long and printed %lx) and %x for
`size-OBMD_HDR`, which is size_t once OBMD_HDR = sizeof(obmd_t) promotes it
(now %zx). In the engine: %d for an off_t (cast to long, %ld) and %x for a
Forth cell, which is a long on the 64-bit engine (%lx). All nine are under
`verbose`/debug paths this build never takes; the point is a clean -Wformat
so a real one is not lost among them. No change to any file written.

Plus one -Wformat-security site, wrapper.c's usage(): printf(help_msg) with
a non-literal format becomes fputs(). Ubuntu's GCC turns -Wformat-security
on by default, so -Werror=format would otherwise stop there.

Applied after engine-tools-c99-decls.patch by build/obp/gnu/engine/Makefile to
a staged copy; src/obp is never touched.

